# URL redirects for Circulation Studio
# See DEPLOYMENT.md for detailed configuration.
#
# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the output root. It reaches _site
# through the passthrough to public/, recorded in DESIGN_SYSTEM.md under Deploy
# pipeline. Plain passthrough copy silently lost it, so if a rule stops working
# check that _site/_redirects still exists before debugging the rule.
#
# FORMAT
#   <from>  <to>  <status>
#
# from    the old path, starting with /. May end in /* to match a subtree, and
#         a :placeholder captures one segment for reuse in <to>.
# to      the new path or a full URL.
# status  301 for a permanent move, which is what a migration wants. 302 only
#         for something genuinely temporary. 200 rewrites without changing the
#         address bar and is not what a migration wants.
#
# Rules are evaluated top to bottom and the FIRST match wins, so the specific
# ones go above the wildcards. A trailing /* rule placed too high swallows every
# specific rule underneath it. There are no wildcards in this file today.


# ============================================================
# THE MIGRATION MAP. COLLECTED 2026-08-17. This is now live.
# ============================================================
#
# SOURCE: the live sitemap at https://www.circulationstudio.com/sitemap.xml,
# fetched 2026-08-17. 41 URLs, none carrying a trailing slash. Nothing in this
# file was reconstructed from memory or derived from the new build, because a
# wrong rule looks exactly like a right one and nothing here can tell the
# difference.
#
# The Search Console backlink export is still outstanding and will add rows that
# the sitemap does not carry. This file is sectioned so those append underneath
# without disturbing anything above them.
#
# WHY EVERY DESTINATION CARRIES A TRAILING SLASH. The build canonicalises to the
# slash form and Cloudflare 308s a bare path to it. A destination without the
# slash would make every one of these a two-hop redirect, which loses a fraction
# of the signal at every hop and is entirely avoidable.
#
# ONE HOP, CHECKED. No destination in this file appears as a source in it.
#
# 41 live URLs account for as follows:
#   32  rules below
#    8  no rule, because this build publishes the same path. Listed at the
#       bottom so the accounting is visible rather than implied.
#    1  no rule, deliberately allowed to 404. Also listed at the bottom.
#
# NO SOURCE PATH COLLIDES WITH A PAGE THIS BUILD PUBLISHES, and that is enforced
# rather than promised: eleventy.config.js fails the build on any rule whose
# source is a built URL. Cloudflare evaluates this file before serving a static
# file, so such a rule would make its own page unreachable with nothing in the
# output to show for it. See the eleventy.after hook.


